## Explanation of the implementation

| Symbol | Rust equivalent |
|--------|------------------|
| `State k = (Layer k, Connections k)` | `struct State { layer: Layer, prev_connections: Vec<Connection> }` – here `prev_connections` stores the mapping that *produced* this layer (from `k-1` to `k`). |
| `Layer k` | `type Layer = Vec<Point>` |
| `N(k+1) = T(N(k))` | `(self.t)(state.layer.len())` – the current layer length is used as `N(k)`. |
| `point(k,i) = G(k, i, N(k))` | `(self.g)(k, i, n_next)` – we pass the current step `k` (interpreted as the layer index), the point index, and the new size. |
| `Connections k = Φ(Layer k, Layer k+1)` | `(self.phi)(&state.layer, &next_layer)` – returns a vector of `(from, to)`. |
| `M(State(k+1)) ≥ M(State(k))` | checked after each step and reported as a boolean. |
| Canonical triple `(T, G, Φ)` | stored as fields of the `Monad` struct. |
| Projections | not explicitly implemented, but you can easily add methods that compute different views (e.g., adjacency matrix, wave‑based transforms). |

